            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.17,
            0.107,
            0.886,
            0.149
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Make a table of values for t varying from 0 to 10 years and show how the population, P, increases every year."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.151,
            0.886,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Find an expression that relates P and t, and explain why it represents linear growth."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.13,
            0.197,
            0.885,
            0.238
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "4. A telecom company charges `600 for a certain recharge scheme. This prepaid balance is reduced by `15 each day after the recharge."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.179,
            0.242,
            0.886,
            0.303
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) Write an equation that models the remaining balance b(x) after using the scheme for x days. Explain why it represents linear decay."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.307,
            0.742,
            0.329
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) After how many days will the balance run out?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.332,
            0.885,
            0.374
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(iii) Make a table of values for x varying from 1 to 10 days and show how the balance b(x), reduces with time."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.39,
            0.477,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2.5 Linear Relationships"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.424,
            0.885,
            0.463
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A linear relationship represents the relationship between two variables x and y, and can be expressed as y = ax + b."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.462,
            0.887,
            0.54
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us revisit the growing pattern of square tiles in Fig. 2.4. If x represents the number of the term and y represents the numbers of square tiles, then the linear relationship between x and y is expressed as y = 2x – 1."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.54,
            0.885,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Sometimes, we may be required to find the linear relationship between two quantities."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.582,
            0.886,
            0.679
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example 11:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A telecom company charges a fixed monthly fee and an additional cost per GB of the internet data used. A student observes that when she used 10 GB, her bill was `350. When she used 20 GB, her bill was `550. If the monthly bill y depends on the amount of data used, x (in GB), according to the relation "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = a x + b ,"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " find the values of a and b."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.679,
            0.884,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Note that x = number of GB of the internet data used and y = total monthly cost in Rupees."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.717,
            0.885,
            0.776
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "To find the linear relationship y = ax + b, we note that when x = 10, y = 350. Also, when x = 20, y = 550. We substitute these in "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "y = ax + b"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to arrive at the following equations."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.326,
            0.779,
            0.672,
            0.798
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_15.jpg",
          "content": "350=10a+b\\ \\text { and }\\ 550=20a+b"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.803,
            0.884,
            0.843
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We solve these as follows: Let b = 350 – 10a (from the first equation). We substitute this in the second equation to obtain"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.373,
            0.845,
            0.624,
            0.865
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_10_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "550 = 20a + (350 - 10a)"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.869,
            0.885,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Thus, 550 = 10a + 350 or 10a = 200. So, a = 20. This leads to b = 350 – 10a = 350 – 200 = 150."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
